  "unknownDispositionRule": {
    "operation": "ReconcileUnknownExecution",
    "request": "exactly {kind, invocation, reason}; there is no isolation, generation, workerId or outcome field, because a request must not be able to answer the question the record exists to settle",
    "evidence": "the Connection and the Worker instance come from the Board's trusted dispatched record for that invocation; the proof that the instance can no longer work comes from the Worker fence in force on that Connection",
    "isolated": "the fence generation in force is strictly greater than the generation recorded on the dispatch record; a Connection with no fence reports generation 0 and is therefore never isolated",
    "isolatedMeans": "shut out of this Board, and nothing more: the fence is a number at the authority, so it does not stop a process, does not reach the Worker host, and does not undo an outward effect the lost instance may already have caused. Whether the world changed is exactly as unknown after the fence as before it. Never state or render this as the old Worker having stopped — an operator who reads that will not take the host out of service.",
    "onAccept": "one immutable execution_unknown row per invocation, carrying the invocation, tool, connection, worker instance, recorded generation, the fence generation that proved isolation, the authenticated operator and the stated reason",
    "onReplay": "a second request for the same invocation writes nothing, bumps no revision and returns the standing record with replay true",
    "affectedCases": "computed from causal reachability as for other writes, not an acknowledgement of reconciliation; an isolated disposition with no causal path to a Case returns an empty array, and replay can leave revision unchanged. Gateway must match the original invocation and the authoritative unknown disposition receipt to release waiting, never infer reconciliation from affectedCases or a revision increment.",
    "releases": "only that this invocation stops blocking a non-completed CloseCase of the roots that reference it; it is not a success, not a failure, certifies nothing, and closes no Case",
    "lateReceipt": "a receipt from the superseded instance is refused by the fence gate with worker_fenced and writes nothing, because the disposition required the fence to have advanced past that instance first",
    "lateReceiptRetention": "not implemented on any side today. Core refuses the late report before any handler and does not journal a refused command, so nothing is retained; the Gateway call ledger has no persistent entry for it either. The approved contract requires a late receipt to stay bound to its original invocation and enter reconciliation, so Gateway adoption must add an audit-only Late-Report record keyed by the original invocation, retained even when Core refuses. That record must never write the live graph and must never enter open obligations, and Core does not reopen graph writes to a superseded Worker for it."
  },
