    "twoTruths": "fence and lease are deliberately two carriers with two field names, because they are two different truths. fence is Core's monotonic record of who holds the line and at which generation; it survives expiry and withdrawal, and null means this Connection has no fence history at all. lease is the Gateway's judgement that a lease is currently valid; null means none is, whether it lapsed, was released, or never existed. Reading either one as the other is how a lapsed lease starts looking like a live one.",
    "rule": "A poll is admitted when no lease is currently valid and the poll states no generation, or when the valid lease belongs to this workerId and any stated generation equals the one it holds. Stating a generation with no valid lease is refused by name: the generation cannot be checked against anything current, and a process that lost the line must take it again the way it did at startup, without stating one. Admission comes first and completely: the Tool Manifest is observed and the Tool lock may move only on an admitted poll, so a refused poll leaves the advertisement and the lock exactly as they were. Poll is the only acquiring verb; claim and report run under a lease and never take one.",
    "generationRule": "An acquisition takes generation 1 only when there is no fence history. Every other acquisition takes a generation strictly higher than the fence already records, whether that fence names a lapsed holder or names none after a withdrawal. Reuse keeps the generation the valid lease already holds, and a refused poll takes none.",
